{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-73686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3y-2z=4 \\\\ -2x-3y=-6 \\\\ x+4z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{y}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+3y+(-2)z=4 \\\\ (-2)x+(-3)y+0z=-6 \\\\ 1x+0y+4z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-73686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+z=1 \\\\ 4x-z=-3 \\\\ x-y+z=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{y}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+(-3)y+1z=1 \\\\ 4x+0y+(-1)z=-3 \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+1z=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-42693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42693" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+5y+z=-9 \\\\ x+y-4z=-1 \\\\ -2x+8y=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+5y+1z=-9 \\\\ 1x+1y+(-4)z=-1 \\\\ -2x+8y+0z=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-9 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|."] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-9 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}-9 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x+6y-z=2 \\\\ 7x-8z=12 \\\\ 3x+5y+z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{z}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(-4)x+6y+(-1)z=2 \\\\ 7x+0y+(-8)z=12 \\\\ 3x+5y+1z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-73688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+7z=14 \\\\ -5x+6y+2z=9 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and ${D}_{z}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+(-5)y+7z=14 \\\\ -5x+6y+2z=9 \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+4z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\nD=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 14 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & -14 \\\\ -5 & 6 & -9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 14 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139985" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 & 14 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-z=1 \\\\ x-2y+2z=3 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $5,$ then $x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+1y+(-1)z=1 \\\\ 1x+(-2)y+2z=3 \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+1z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-(-4))-(3-4)-(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & =2+1+2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{5}{5}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y-z=1 \\\\ 2x-3z=-2 \\\\ -x+y-2z=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $42,$ then $x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y+(-1)z=1 \\\\ 2x+0y+(-3)z=-2 \\\\ (-1)x+1y+(-2)z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|=42.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0+3)-5(4+18)-(-2-0) \\\\  & =3-110+2 \\\\  & =-105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{-105}{42}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-42623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+z=5 \\\\ x+y-2z=-3 \\\\ -5x+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $7,$ then $y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+(-3)y+1z=5 \\\\ 1x+1y+(-2)z=-3 \\\\ -5x+0y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{y},$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(-12-2)-5(4-10)+(-1-15) \\\\  & =-70+30-16 \\\\  & =-56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-56}{7}=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-42671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-42671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y+3z=-2 \\\\ 2x-y=3 \\\\ -x-2y+z=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-18,$ then $x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1x+1y+3z=-2 \\\\ 2x+(-1)y+0z=3 \\\\ (-1)x+(-2)y+1z=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(-1-0)-(3-0)-(-6+6) \\\\  & =2-3-0 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{-1}{-18}=\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{18}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73690" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{18}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y+2z=-2 \\\\ 2x-5y+1z=-10 \\\\ 2x+y-2z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $66,$ then $y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y+2z=-2 \\\\ 2x+(-5)y+1z=-10 \\\\ 2x+1y+(-2)z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|=66\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{y},$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the second column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-10 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(20+1)+2(-4-2)+2(-2+20) \\\\  & =42-12+36 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{66}{66}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-139987" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y-z=1 \\\\ x+4y+kz=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y+4z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $z=1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $97-21k,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|=97-21k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $z$ is given by $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 9\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(36+3)+3(9+2)+(3-8) \\\\  & =195+33-5 \\\\  & =223.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{223}{97-21k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $z=1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{223}{97-21k} & =1 \\\\ 223 & =97-21k \\\\ 21k & =-126 \\\\ k & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-6"] ["math" "k=1"] ["math" "k=4"] ["math" "k=5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-140043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ 4x-5y+kz=1 \\\\ -2x+10y-5z=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $160-70k,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-140043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -5 & k \\\\ -2 & 10 & -5\\end{aligned}|=160-70k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & k \\\\ -2 & 10 & -5\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-5 & k \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(25-10k)-5(-5+2k)-3(10-10) \\\\  & =50-20k+25-10k+0 \\\\  & =75-30k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{75-30k}{160-70k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{75-30k}{160-70k} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2(75-30k) & =160-70k \\\\ 150-60k & =160-70k \\\\ 10k & =10 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-140043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-140043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-140043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-4"] ["math" "k=1"] ["math" "k=11"] ["math" "k=2"] ["math" "k=9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-140043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+z=3 \\\\ x-z=k \\\\ x-2y+2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $z=2$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-15,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $z$ is given by $z=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & k \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+2k)-3(1-k)+3(-2-0) \\\\  & =4k-3+3k-6 \\\\  & =7k-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{7k-9}{-15}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $z=2.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7k-9}{-15} & =2 \\\\ 7k-9 & =-30 \\\\ 7k & =-21 \\\\ k & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-73694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-2"] ["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-4"] ["math" "k=3"] ["math" "k=7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+2z=6 \\\\ 3x+2y-z=k \\\\ 4x+3y-3z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $x=1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-9,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ k & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-6+3)+(-3k+1)+2(3k-2) \\\\  & =-18-3k+1+6k-4 \\\\  & =3k-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{3k-21}{-9}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9}{3k-21} & =1 \\\\ -9 & =3k-21 \\\\ 12 & =3k \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-43113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-1"] ["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-9"] ["math" "k=4"] ["math" "k=5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-43113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+2z=k \\\\ x+y=-1 \\\\ y+z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $y=-5$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $1,$ find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1-0)-k(1-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =-2-k+4 \\\\  & =2-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{2-k}{1}=2-k.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=-5.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-k & =-5 \\\\ k & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73698" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a1a6979836a56791792e28734dc7b6d21137040e0b92775cd68600d8dd8033e4"} {"question" "q-73698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-3"] ["math" "k=-7"] ["math" "k=2"] ["math" "k=3"] ["math" "k=7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "q-73698" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4e6a245ac99e3861b497f4684f4824d5e3fca93ae24639c3e300750dfc43b13"} {"question" "e-6172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-6z=8 \\\\ -6x+4y+2z=3 \\\\ 5x-5y-15z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $x=\\dfrac{D_x}{D}$, where $D$ is the determinant of the coefficient matrix and $D_x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/example-6172.json" "file_sha256" "a709eb8c341aaea00a2a32028143a125b583ff9b6a1078376b4ab70e960dd497"} {"question" "e-6172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9x+3y+(-6)z=8 \\\\ (-6)x+4y+2z=3 \\\\ 5x+(-5)y+(-15)z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/assets/00a69fe1d48b41e376971f3669ae51668733d36dfda18c0f9cc736d5d071a441.png)\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/assets/14e850c9af7c0b2fdd1e36299667b2cbe91c84e8bb90030b729ee23b296ad984.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/example-6172.json" "file_sha256" "a709eb8c341aaea00a2a32028143a125b583ff9b6a1078376b4ab70e960dd497"} {"question" "e-4577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. Find $z.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4x-2z=1 \\\\ 3x+y-z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/example-4577.json" "file_sha256" "333f3e960bcc067cf17472163594e62ac6d5414f0dbb528b9374219b4a7551e2"} {"question" "e-4577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1x-1y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4x+0y-2z=1 \\\\ 3x+1y-1z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(-4+6)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =2+2+12 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find $D_z,$ we take the coefficients matrix, replace the *third* column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-1)+(-8-3)-(4-0) \\\\  & =-1-11-4 \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{-16}{16}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/example-4577.json" "file_sha256" "333f3e960bcc067cf17472163594e62ac6d5414f0dbb528b9374219b4a7551e2"} {"question" "e-4579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. Given that $x = 2,$ find the value of $k.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=-1 \\\\ kx+3y-2z=1 \\\\ 3x-y+2z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/example-4579.json" "file_sha256" "ea0bad510dc4dff86485f9480acabda17cb593eeb1e0b65e06a2da7233011cd4"} {"question" "e-4579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ k & 3 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6-2)-2(2k+6)-(-k-9) \\\\  & =4-4k-12+k+9 \\\\  & =1-3k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x = \\dfrac{D_x}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(6-2)-2(2+6)-(-1-9) \\\\  & =-4-16+10 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{D_x}{D} = \\dfrac{-10}{1-3k}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=2.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-10}{1-3k} & =2 \\\\ -10 & =2-6k \\\\ 6k & =12 \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059591/example-4579.json" "file_sha256" "ea0bad510dc4dff86485f9480acabda17cb593eeb1e0b65e06a2da7233011cd4"} {"question" "q-42681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" 